INT. UNDERGROUND SQUASH COURT - NIGHT

A glass-backed court under a bare basement vault. Brick pillars, pipes, one hanging fluorescent. A banner on the back wall: CITY SQUASH LEAGUE FINALS - TIED 2-2.

COACH WINIFRED BAPTISTE (50s, weathered, towel around her neck) kneels at the sidewall, tying a young player's shoe. TOMASINA "TOMMIE" VAUGHN (20s, wiry, headband) bounces a ball against the front wall, thwack, thwack, thwack.

COACH BAPTISTE
(to the court)
Fifteen minutes. Hydrate.

TOMMIE
Coach, I'm fine.

COACH BAPTISTE
I wasn't talking to you.

TOMMIE
Then who?

COACH BAPTISTE
The universe.

Tommie laughs. The ball rebounds. She catches it one-handed.

COACH BAPTISTE (CONT'D)
Tommie. Listen.

TOMMIE
I'm listening.

COACH BAPTISTE
She hits down the wall on every second serve. You know it.

TOMMIE
I know it.

COACH BAPTISTE
Cut it off at the T.

TOMMIE
At the T.

COACH BAPTISTE
And don't go chasing winners. Wait for her to give you one.

The glass door at the back of the court swings open. A tall woman in a navy tracksuit enters, bag over one shoulder, the quiet confidence of someone who has never lost in this building. This is LENORE ASHCROFT (40s, former national champion, silver in her hair).

LENORE
Winnie.

COACH BAPTISTE
(without turning)
Lenore.

LENORE
Heard you had a final.

COACH BAPTISTE
Heard you were retired.

LENORE
I am. I'm here to watch.

COACH BAPTISTE
Sit anywhere. Not in my line of sight.

Lenore smiles and takes a seat in the gallery, high up in the dark. Tommie looks from one to the other. The ball stops.

TOMMIE
Who's that?

COACH BAPTISTE
My old partner.

TOMMIE
She looks like she's judging me.

COACH BAPTISTE
She is.

TOMMIE
(muttering)
Great. Great.

COACH BAPTISTE
(to the court)
Fifteen minutes. Hydrate.

LENORE
(calling from the gallery)
Hit the wall, Tommie. Not the ball.

Tommie looks up. A long pause. Then she turns to the front wall and lets the ball go.
